    fix(data-quality): enhance OHLCV validation and signal integrity

    Refined the OHLCV data validation process by implementing a centralized helper function to drop invalid bars (NaN, zero, negative values) across various components. This ensures that all price data entering the system is sanitized, preventing corrupt signals and erroneous price readings. Updated relevant methods in SignalEngine and trading scripts to utilize the new validation logic, improving overall data integrity and reliability of market signals. All tests pass successfully, confirming the effectiveness of these changes.

